          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.089,
            0.847,
            0.147
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. The hypotenuse of an isosceles right triangle is 10. What are its other two sidelengths? ["
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find the area of the square composed of two such right triangles.]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.162,
            0.337,
            0.181
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "General Solution"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.185,
            0.847,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The relation between the areas of a square and the square on its diagonal can be used to find a general relation between the hypotenuse and the other two sides of an isosceles right triangle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.348,
            0.247,
            0.685,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.348,
                0.247,
                0.685,
                0.504
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.509,
            0.845,
            0.53
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let a be the length of the equal sides and c the length of the hypotenuse."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.34,
            0.533,
            0.66,
            0.553
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Area of SQVU = 2 × Area of PQRS"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.419,
            0.556,
            0.531,
            0.577
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "S 0 , c ^ { 2 } = 2 \\bar { a } ^ { 2 }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.581,
            0.845,
            0.62
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This formula can be used to find c when a is known, or to find a when c is known."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.629,
            0.845,
            0.669
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find the hypotenuse of an isosceles right triangle whose equal sides have length 12."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.672,
            0.562,
            0.693
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = 1 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Using the formula, we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.395,
            0.7,
            0.6,
            0.724
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "c = \\sqrt{2 \\times 12^{2}} = \\sqrt{288}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.732,
            0.476,
            0.753
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 6 ^ { 2 } = 2 5 6"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 7 ^ { 2 } = 2 8 9"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.757,
            0.474,
            0.778
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\sqrt { 2 8 8 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " lies between 16 and 17."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.782,
            0.846,
            0.822
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The length of the hypotenuse of an isosceles right triangle, whose length of the equal sides is 12 units, is between 16 and 17 units."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.83,
            0.846,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Example 2: If the hypotenuse of an isosceles right triangle is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\sqrt { 7 2 } } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " find its other two sides."
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.873,
            0.573,
            0.894
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "c = { \\sqrt { 7 2 } } ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Using the formula, we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.462,
            0.896,
            0.537,
            0.916
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "c ^ { 2 }   = 2 a ^ { 2 }"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
